# ---------- M0 spike ----------
# Throwaway code whose only job is to answer questions about polkit, D-Bus and SSE.
# ADR-0011 commits to deleting it, and names the risk that a working spike gets
# promoted to production instead. Making it uncommittable is the cheapest enforcement
# available. Findings belong in ADRs; the code does not belong in the repository.
spike/

# ---------- Machine-local tooling ----------
# Per-machine Claude Code settings: permission allowlists containing absolute
# paths and local usernames. Shared project config (.claude/settings.json,
# .claude/agents/, .claude/commands/) is deliberately NOT ignored — it belongs
# in the repository.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# ---------- Secrets & local config ----------
# The agent's runtime state (device registry, token hashes, audit log) and any
# real service credentials must never be committed. See ADR-0006.
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml
config.yaml
!config.example.yaml
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.pem
!**/testdata/**/*.key

# ---------- Go ----------
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
/agent/bin/
/agent/dist/
/dist/
go.work
go.work.sum
coverage.out
coverage.html

# ---------- Android / Gradle / Kotlin ----------
.gradle/
build/
captures/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.aar
*.ap_
*.dex
*.jks
*.keystore
!debug.keystore
.cxx/
lint-results*.html
lint-results*.xml
# Screenshot-test output (Paparazzi). Golden images ARE committed; failures are not.
**/src/test/snapshots/**/*_delta.png
out/

# ---------- Generated code ----------
# Generated from api/openapi.yaml. Committed deliberately so the CI drift gate can
# diff regenerated output against the tree — see ADR-0009. Nothing is ignored here
# on purpose; this block is a signpost, not a rule.

# ---------- IDE & editors ----------
.idea/
!.idea/codeStyles/
*.iml
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ---------- OS ----------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Stray runtime files from local testing
*.pid

# Local scratch: agent doubles, screenshots and test databases used by hand.
.demo/

# ---------- Local deployment scratch ----------
# Staging scripts, cross-compiled binaries and device screenshots produced while
# verifying a phase against the real host. The reusable parts belong in deploy/;
# what lands here is per-session and names local paths.
.deploy/

# ---------- Release output ----------
# Where scripts/release-agent.sh assembles the tarball. Build output, reproducible
# from any tag, and an 18 MB binary that would be committed by accident exactly once.
dist/

# ---------- Scratch captures from hardware sessions ----------
# Screenshots pulled off the watch or the test VM console while verifying a phase.
# They are how a claim gets checked, not evidence worth keeping: the finding belongs
# in the plan or a verification record, in words. One slipped into a docs commit on
# 2026-09-21 via `git add -A`, and one of that session's frames had the VM's sudo
# password echoed on screen — this one did not, but the next one might.
.vmshot.png
.watch.png

# ---------- Third-party agent skills ----------
# Installed by `npx skills add`, which drops them in the project directory. They are
# machine-local tooling in the same sense as .claude/settings.local.json: useful for
# working on CueSeek, not part of it. Vendoring 600 files of someone else's design
# library into this repository would add a licence surface and a maintenance burden for
# something reinstallable in one command.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json
